From: Ray Liu <ray.xy.liu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 02:18:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: eth - drop no_npu CDM1 bypass for AN7563

The previous patch (613) forced airoha_dev_open() to forward GDM
traffic directly to FE_PSE_PORT_CDM1 (QDMA CPU DMA), bypassing PPE,
on the assumption that AN7563 had no usable NPU bring-up path. That
turned out to be incorrect - the EcoNet GPL drop ships a tiny but
fully functional NPU firmware blob (~90 KB rv32 + ~3 KB data) and
the AN7563 NPU MMIO block is register-compatible with EN7581
(verified against the GPL ecnt_npu.c source).

With the new airoha,an7563-npu DT compatible (patch 614) and the
airoha-an7563-npu-firmware package wired in, the upstream
airoha_ppe_offload_setup() -> NPU bring-up path now runs on AN7563,
so we no longer need to short-circuit GDM_FWD_CFG. Drop the CDM1
bypass and let airoha_dev_open() use its normal FE_PSE_PORT_PPE1
route.

Signed-off-by: Ray Liu <ray.xy.liu@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3584,7 +3584,13 @@ static const struct airoha_eth_soc_data
 	.num_xsi_rsts = ARRAY_SIZE(en7581_xsi_rsts_names),
 	.num_ppe = 1,
 	.ppe_skip_flush_sram = true,
-	.no_npu = true,
+	/*
+	 * With airoha,an7563-npu node + an7563_npu_{rv32,data}.bin
+	 * firmware in place, the upstream PPE/NPU bring-up path now
+	 * runs, so we do NOT need to bypass PPE via CDM1 forwarding.
+	 * Keep .no_npu = false (default) so airoha_dev_open() uses
+	 * the standard FE_PSE_PORT_PPE1 route.
+	 */
 	/*
 	 * AN7563 silicon shares the EN7581 frame-engine and source-port
 	 * encoding (verified against the GPL en7523.dtsi and Xiaomi
